raye-wine (11.21-1~raye3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Windows programs no longer bring up the screen share picker on their
    own. It comes after a click or a key in the program, within 5 seconds,
    from a menu item or a global hotkey, or when the program keeps reading
    the screen like a recorder. Discord and Roblox Studio start without it.
  * Screen capture works with Plasma's share picker: one source is asked
    for, and a whole-desktop share gives each screen its own part.
  * OBS Studio 33 for Windows starts and records.
  * The MIDI mapper is called Microsoft MIDI Mapper, PipeWire's own MIDI
    bridge is no longer listed, and an input that fails to connect is not
    left marked as in use.
  * crypt32 answers a certificate's SHA-256 thumbprint (Paint.NET's
    installer asks for it).
  * The mouse, keyboard, ACM codecs, DirectDraw devices, MCI players, the
    C++ runtime error box and WMI devices no longer show the old project
    name.
  * Ships raye-windows-titles, the per-title answers and the Roblox
    profiles; it says before anything runs that the Windows Minecraft
    launcher and Bedrock can't work, and points to Java in the Store.
  * New raye-wine-compat, which gives winetricks the wine it asks for.
  * Raye ASIO switches the sound to 44.1 kHz when a program asks for it,
    FL Studio's default, and PipeWire may run at 44.1 or 48 kHz.
  * Depends on PipeWire's JACK library and the GStreamer plugins Windows
    programs play media through.
  * Direct2D custom effects work and color contexts are made instead of
    refused, so Paint.NET's installer gets past its graphics check.
  * A hidden window stays hidden when the window manager answers late.
  * Roblox Studio runs with mimalloc in place of malloc.

 -- techoraye <190692880+techoraye@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:38:14 +0000

